---
code: cfg-builtin-shadowed
when-fires: a book funcdef shadows a shell builtin the engine relies on (dash resolves a function before a regular builtin). cfg.rs warn_shadowed_relied_builtins.
why: find-I: builtin-dependent conclusions may be unsound for this book. The hole is typed: `{name}` is the shadowing function, which is also the builtin it shadows; the sentence is the code's own register. The primary span is the funcdef name_span.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- cfg-builtin-shadowed && mise run loom:promote -- cfg-builtin-shadowed`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all cfg-builtin-shadowed` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
test() { hork --stub; }
if test -f /etc/nginx/nginx.conf; then
  apt-get install -y nginx
fi

-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh
warning[cfg-builtin-shadowed]: Function `test` shadows a shell builtin Dorc
relies on: analysis keeps reading the bare word `test` as the builtin, so
conclusions that lean on it may be unsound for this book.
      [ book.sh:2:1
   2 | test() { hork --stub; }
     | \__/
